---
import { SITE } from '@/config';
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Contact"
  description={`Report an error, suggest a problem to cover, or reach the editor of ${SITE.name}.`}
  path="/contact"
  lede="Corrections get priority. We would rather be right than look right."
>
  <aside class="callout alert">
    <div class="eyebrow">Never send us these</div>
    <p>
      Do not send account numbers, card numbers, CVV, PIN, OTP, passwords, or photographs of
      statements and cheques. We do not need them, we cannot act on your account, and nobody
      legitimate will ask you for them. If someone claiming to be from this site asks, it is fraud.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> reaches the editor. We read everything and
    reply to most things within a few working days.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting an error</h2>
  <p>
    Include the page URL and, if you can, the circular or document that says otherwise. Substantive
    corrections are made with a visible note on the page, as set out in the
    <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Suggesting a topic</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us what went wrong, what you tried, and where you got stuck. Specific, awkward problems are
    the most useful — those are the ones nobody has written up properly.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact your bank for you, or escalate a complaint on your behalf.</li>
    <li>Tell you which product to buy for your personal situation.</li>
    <li>Recover money, reverse a transaction, or influence a bank's decision.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For those, the route is your bank's grievance redressal officer and then the RBI Ombudsman.
    <a href="/disputes"> We explain how that ladder works</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Press and partnerships</h2>
  <p>
    Same address. We do not publish sponsored posts or sell links — see the
    <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
